{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>El Ro'i.</b> On the pattern of רָאָה עָנִי (Lamentations 3:1), in the sense of El of seeing." "<b>Hagam halom.</b> Like \"now.\" But the correct view is that it is like \"here,\" as in \"Is there yet a man who comes here?\" (1 Samuel 10:22). And the meaning is: Have I even here seen the angel of HaShem, after HaShem saw my affliction — for He is the One who sees always."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:48.967859456Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}